<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Günther XLI of Schwarzburg-Arnstadt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1529–1583</span> · Also known as Günther the Warlike</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Günther XLI, called the Warlike, was a count of Schwarzburg who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnstadt">Arnstadt</a>. He served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as a military commander, including in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, and was one of the leading German Protestant nobles in imperial service. His death without children in 1583 led to a period of joint rule and the division of the Schwarzburg lands in 1599.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gunther-xli-of-schwarzburg-arnstadt.jpg" alt="Günther XLI of Schwarzburg-Arnstadt" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, possibly Antonis Mor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%BCnther_der_Streitbare_als_junger_Oberst.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
